{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Evidence pass over all 12 failed Reconcile Bridge runs (2026-08-06 -> 2026-08-11). The Mode 2 framing in the description is REFUTED; Mode 1 is confirmed.\n\nMODE 1 — CONFIRMED, 6/12 runs terminating (31481490100, 31358521998, 31350775907, 31263067299, 31222668500, 31179770156). Identical in all six: fails on the VERY FIRST ACLI call (jira workitem search --jql ...), 15-20s after 'Reconciling in/with mode: live', with NO reconcile work preceding it. The 'acli jira auth login' step earlier in the job SUCCEEDED (cache hit acli-Linux-1.3.19-stable, no login error). So the token is rejected at FIRST USE, not at login — i.e. the JIRA_API_TOKEN secret value is expired/revoked, not a session dying mid-pass.\n\nMODE 2 — REFUTED as a failure cause, 0/12 runs terminating. 'command cancelled' is non-fatal stderr NOISE inside the outbound link-apply loop. It first appears right after 'RECON: typed_inbound_dispatched count=16' (or 19), 2-6 min in, and each occurrence is bracketed by a SUCCESSFUL 'RECON: batch_outcome action=update key=REB-... error=None links_applied=N'. No exit code, no HTTP status, no traceback, no reconciler-level ERROR attached. The enclosing operation is recorded as succeeding.\n\nThe 6 runs the sweep attributed to Mode 2 actually died in GIT DELIVERY, in three unrelated classes:\n  - TLS: 'server certificate verification failed. CAfile: none CRLfile: none' (31535962079 push-transport-failed, 3 unpushed commits; 31420498173 merge-recovery-blocked, 2 unpushed)\n  - Ref push rejected: 31455622724 stale --force-with-lease on refs/reconciler/last-pass; 31244501098 lost race on refs/heads/tickets ('is at e45f61a9 but expected 9ecaaa40', 6 unpushed)\n  - Re-dispatch: 31129551929 + 31129431096, 'HTTP 422: Cannot trigger a workflow_dispatch on a disabled workflow'\n\nAC3 ANSWERED, opposite to the hypothesis: Mode 1 and Mode 2 are INDEPENDENT. 'unauthorized' count is 0 in all six Mode-2-noise runs; the two signatures never co-occur. Mode 2 is not the expiry surfacing mid-pass.\n\nAC4 is MOOT: no pass is aborted by Mode 2, so there is no partially-applied reconcile from that cause.\n\nCODE DEFECT FOUND for Mode 1 reporting, in src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py: the auth fast-abort is keyed on '_AUTH_FAILURE_CODE = 401' / 'if cpe.returncode == _AUTH_FAILURE_CODE'. ACLI is a subprocess and exits 1, never 401, so that branch is DEAD CODE. An expired credential is therefore retried 3x with backoff (pointless — it is deterministic) and then surfaces as the generic 'reconcile_once raised: ... returned non-zero exit status 1'. Nothing in rebar_reconciler/ matches the 'unauthorized' / 'auth login' stderr string.\n\nSCOPE DECISION. AC1's RENEWAL half is not achievable in code: since the token is rejected at first use, re-running 'acli jira auth login' with the same JIRA_API_TOKEN cannot help. Renewal requires ROTATING the secret — an ops action needing a new secret value, deliberately not attempted here. This ticket will deliver the detection/reporting half (AC2) as a self-contained fix; the git-delivery failures and the swallowed 'command cancelled' noise will be filed as separate linked tickets."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786516820486312001,"uuid":"7526a77a-de54-4886-ba99-c291b16e180c"}